    <!-- How to connect -->
    <string name="connect_help">How to connect</string>
    <string name="connect_help_body"><![CDATA[<b>You need</b> a running Kiro Crew gateway. Your phone must reach it over Tailscale, the same Wi‑Fi, or HTTPS.<br><br>
<b>Fast way: scan a QR code</b><br>
1. On your computer, open the Kiro Crew dashboard.<br>
2. Open <b>Connect your phone</b>.<br>
3. In this app, tap <b>Scan QR code</b> and point at the code.<br>
The app saves the server and signs you in.<br><br>
<b>Or type the address</b><br>
1. Tap <b>Add server</b>.<br>
2. Type the dashboard address and tap <b>Save</b>.<br>
3. Sign in on the page that opens.<br><br>
<b>Address examples</b><br>
• Tailscale: <tt>http://my-host.tailnet.ts.net:5476</tt><br>
• Same Wi‑Fi: <tt>http://192.168.1.20:5476</tt><br>
• Own domain: <tt>https://kiro.example.com</tt><br>
<tt>host:5476</tt> becomes <tt>http://</tt>. A plain domain becomes <tt>https://</tt>.<br><br>
<b>Will not connect?</b><br>
• Check Tailscale is on, on both the phone and the gateway.<br>
• Check the port (default 5476).<br>
• The gateway must listen beyond localhost to be reached from the phone.<br>
• A sign-in page that keeps coming back: make a fresh QR code.]]></string>
